# {{display_name}}

{{description}}

A [BTCPay Server](https://btcpayserver.org) plugin written in Rust with
[btcpay-rs](https://github.com/uqlidi/btcpay-rs). All the logic lives in `src/lib.rs`;
the C# that BTCPay actually loads is generated at build time and is not part of this
repository.

## Requirements

- Rust 1.88 or newer
- .NET SDK 10.0, to build the generated shim

## Developing

```sh
cargo build            # compile the plugin
cargo test             # run your tests
cargo btcpay package   # produce an installable .btcpay
```

The first build fetches a BTCPay Server checkout, because `BTCPayServer.Abstractions` is
not published on NuGet. It is cached, so only the first build pays for it. Change which
version you target in `btcpay.toml`.

## Installing

Upload the file from `artifacts/` in BTCPay under Server Settings, Plugins, then restart
BTCPay. Plugins load once at startup, so a restart is required after installing or
upgrading.

## Where things live

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `src/lib.rs` | your plugin |
| `btcpay.toml` | which BTCPay version to build against, and target platforms |
| `artifacts/` | the packaged plugin (generated) |
| `target/` | build output, including the generated C# (generated) |

Identity (identifier, name, version) comes from the attribute in `src/lib.rs` and from
`Cargo.toml`. There is no second copy anywhere, so nothing can fall out of step.
